{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Wait for me</b> — Most of the commentators interpreted it: wait for me a little, and they say: for it is like כתרו את בנימן. It is also possible that כתרו means 'surrounded him,' for כתר and עטרה are close in meaning, as in עוטרים את דוד. And likewise: מכתיר את הצדיק. And likewise: בי יכתירו צדיקים, and its meaning would be: כתר לי — grant me a little honor."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:37.088890861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}